cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use DawnDock in work you publish, please cite it.
title: "DawnDock: a multi-engine GUI application for molecular docking with deep learning scoring"
version: "1.0.0"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ahmed
    given-names: Sk. Faisal
    affiliation: "Dawn of Bioinformatics Ltd., Bangladesh"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9299-1240"
    email: dawn.of.bioinformatics@gmail.com
abstract: >-
  DawnDock is a free Windows desktop application for molecular docking. It runs
  five docking engines from one window, including GNINA, which scores poses
  with a convolutional neural network rather than with a classical scoring
  function alone. It covers receptor and ligand preparation, search box
  definition, docking, pose inspection in 3D and export, without a command
  line.
keywords:
  - molecular docking
  - virtual screening
  - drug discovery
  - structure-based drug design
  - bioinformatics
  - cheminformatics
  - deep learning
  - convolutional neural network
  - GNINA
  - AutoDock Vina
  - protein-ligand interaction
  - Windows
  - desktop application
  - Bangladesh
